      "extract": "We recall some classical results (a modern proof is given in [vdP-S1]). The classiﬁcation of regular singular modules over K and \u0003K are similar and we restrict our attention to q-diﬀerence modules M over K. A diﬀerence module over K is called regular singular if there exists a lattice M 0 ⊂M over C{z} (i.e., M 0 = C{z}e1 ⊕· · ·⊕C{z}em for some K-basis {e1, . . . , em} of M) which is invariant under Φ and Φ−1 (or in",
      "extractCut": true
