      "extract": "We describe here the slope ﬁltration and give references for more details and proofs. It is well known that any diﬀerence module M over K contains a cyclic vector. This means that there exists an element e ∈M such that the homomorphism K[Φ, Φ−1] →M, given by \u0002 anΦn \u0004→\u0002 anΦn(e), is surjec- tive (compare Lemma 4.1). Thus M is isomorphic to K[Φ, Φ−1]/K[Φ, Φ−1]L for some L of the form Φd+ad−1Φd−1+· · ·+a0, with all ai",
      "extractCut": true
