      "extract": "Let F ⊂G be a ﬁnite extension of diﬀerence ﬁelds. Let M be a diﬀerence module over G. Then Res(M) (the restriction of M to F) denotes M, considered as a diﬀerence module over F. One observes that dimF Res(M) = [G : F] · dimG M. Put \u0003Kn = \u0003K(z1/n) for any integer n ⩾1. We apply the above restriction to the extension \u0003K ⊂\u0003Kn in order to construct all irreducible modules over \u0003K. Consider integers t, n with n ⩾1 and",
