      "extract": "K∞denotes the algebraic closure of K and Gal denotes the Galois group of K∞/K. Let M be a diﬀerence module over K∞. Descent data D for M means a map σ ∈Gal \u0004→D(σ) satisfying: D(σ) is a σ-linear bijection on M, D(σ) commutes with Φ, D(σ1)D(σ2) = D(σ1σ2) and the stabilizer of any m ∈M, i.e., the group {σ ∈Gal | D(σ)m = m}, is an open subgroup of Gal. One associates to a diﬀerence module N over K the module M := K∞⊗ N",
