      "extract": "We recall that O denotes the algebra of the holomorphic functions on C∗and that a diﬀerence module M over O is a left module over the ring O[Φ, Φ−1], free of some rank m < ∞over O. Further pr : C∗→Eq := C∗/qZ denotes the canonical map. One associates to M the vector bundle v(M) of rank m on Eq given by v(M)(U) = {f ∈O(pr−1U)⊗OM| Φ(f) = f}, where, for any open V ⊂C∗, O(V ) is the algebra of the holomorphic functions",
